# Proposed by the swarm's review (2026-10-14); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a wide Preview window floats while Safari docks beside it. Preview makes
# way, stays in view when the Desktop is squeezed into a tile, and is left alone
# where its owner puts it on purpose.
# Reference: T03 T08 T50.
open Safari 440x400
open Preview 1000x500
dock 101 left
# Preview is pushed off the space Safari took.
expect left-of 101 102
expect visible 102
# Safari's edge is pulled across the Desktop until it is too narrow to use. Only a move
# of the view takes a window out of view, so Preview stays.
resize 101 right 500
expect visible 102
# A look at Safari on its own takes Preview out of view. Back where the Desktop is part of the view, if only as a
# tile, Preview is in view again.
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
back
expect visible 102
# ⌘Tab to Preview from the framed Safari opens the Desktop rather than leaving it out of view.
zoom 101
flush
focus 102
expect camera desktop
expect visible 102
back
back
resize 101 right -500
expect visible 102
expect left-of 101 102
# Put half over Safari on purpose, it stays there when something else changes.
open Notes
dock 103 right
move 102 500 300 400 300
minimize 103
restore 103
expect visible 102
expect left-of 102 103
# Floating a window out of a column puts it on the Desktop, not over its old neighbour. (It has its own size
# back, F48, and fits. One wider than the Desktop hangs over: 48-float-gets-its-size-back.sim.)
open Mail
dock 104 beside 101 bottom
float 101
expect floating 101
expect size 101 440x400
expect left-of 104 101
